\title{Normal extension}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{An extension #{L/K} is \em{normal} if it is algebraic and the minimal polynomial of every #{\alpha \in L} splits into linear factors over #{L}.}

\p{Equivalently, if #{f \in K[X]} is irreducible and has a root in #{L}, then it splits into linear factors over #{L}. (Slogan: “one out, all out”.)}
